Open Threads

- Exact RPC provider contracts/partnerships — not publicly disclosed; network inspection only shows endpoints, not commercial relationships
- Cloud/CDN provider identity — not publicly disclosed; inferred from headers/network traffic only
- Jupiter integration depth — whether Pump.fun uses only Jupiter Swap API or also Limit Order / DCA / Perps features; not documented
- Jito integration scope — whether all transactions route through Jito or only opt-in; tip amount strategy; not documented
- WalletConnect / Wallet Adapter version — which specific wallets are tested/supported beyond the major ones; no compatibility matrix published
- Third-party indexer relationships — whether Pump.fun runs its own indexer or uses The Graph / Goldsky / Helius / Triton indexers; not documented
- Mobile app backend — whether mobile apps share the same API/indexer as web or have separate infrastructure; not documented
- PumpSwap on Blast confirmation — Blastscan contract address placeholder used; need verified contract address and deployment transaction
- Base/Blast RPC provider specifics — which providers for which chain; not documented
- Block explorer data licensing — whether Pump.fun has commercial agreements with Solscan/SolanaFM/Basescan or uses free tiers
- Apple/Google policy compliance — whether Pump.fun has faced app review rejections or policy warnings; not publicly disclosed
- Regulatory counsel / legal entity — whether any law firm or compliance partner engaged; not disclosed
- Bug bounty / security partner — whether private bug bounty exists with Immunefi/HackerOne or audit firm on retainer; not found on public platforms
- Community dashboard maintenance — whether Pump.fun officially endorses or supports any Dune/Flipside dashboards; not documented
- Cross-chain bridge partnerships — whether Pump.fun recommends specific bridges (Wormhole, LayerZero, deBridge) for users moving assets; not documented
- Fee collector multisig signers — identity and number of signers for fee collector addresses on all three chains; not verified
- Upgrade authority multisig signers — identity and threshold for program/contract upgrade keys on all three chains; not verified